.TH BENTOPACK-CLI 1 "October 2026" "BentoPack 0.11.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bentopack-cli \- headless 2D sprite atlas packer, smart slicer, image filter, and game engine asset compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bentopack-cli
[\fIGLOBAL_OPTIONS\fR] [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIINPUT_FILES\fR...]
.br
.B bentopack-cli
\-\-sheet \fISHEET_FILE\fR \-\-data \fIDATA_FILE\fR [\fIPACK_OPTIONS\fR] [\fIINPUT_FILES\fR...]
.br
.B TexturePacker
[\fITEXTUREPACKER_COMPATIBLE_OPTIONS\fR] [\fIINPUT_FILES\fR...]
.br
.B aseprite
\-b [\fIASEPRITE_COMPATIBLE_OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bentopack-cli
is the non-interactive, headless command-line tool of the BentoPack 2D sprite suite.
It executes without any graphic display server or X11/Wayland dependencies (\fBQT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen\fR),
making it ideal for CI/CD automation, game engine asset pipelines, and AI coding agents.
.PP
The tool features an automatic flavor dispatcher allowing it to act either as a native CLI
or as a seamless 100% drop-in replacement for \fBTexturePacker\fR and \fBAseprite\fR batch scripts.

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display syntax summary and command help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display application version and engine information.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit structured JSON output to standard output (ideal for scripting and AI agents).
.TP
.B \-\-schema
Emit complete self-describing JSON Schema of all commands, options, and capabilities for AI agents.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress progress and status logs, emitting only critical errors or clean JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Display verbose debug information during execution.
.TP
.BI \-\-flavor " <tp|aseprite|godot|native>"
Force command line syntax flavor regardless of binary name.

.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B pack
Pack loose sprites, directories, or project files into an optimized texture atlas.
.TP
.B slice
Extract individual sprite frames from raw composite sheets using smart connected-component detection.
.TP
.B filter
Apply non-destructive image filters (despill, outline, color-swap, color-adjust, pixel-rescale).
.TP
.B bento\fR, \fBssp
Inspect, unpack, or export native BentoPack project archives (\fB.bento\fR).
.TP
.B schema
Output the machine-readable capability manifest and JSON schema for AI agents.

.SH PACKING OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-sheet " <file>"
Destination sprite sheet image (e.g. \fIatlas.png\fR, \fIatlas.ktx2\fR, \fIatlas.basis\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-data " <file>"
Destination descriptor metadata (e.g. \fIatlas.json\fR, \fIatlas.tres\fR, \fIatlas.unity.json\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-format " <fmt>"
Export metadata format: \fBjson-array\fR, \fBjson-hash\fR, \fBgodot4\fR, \fBunity\fR, \fBunreal\fR, \fBlibgdx\fR, \fBspine\fR, \fBbento\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-algorithm " <algo>"
Packing algorithm: \fBMaxRects\fR (default), \fBBasic\fR (RowPacker), \fBGrid\fR, \fBTightPolygon\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-maxrects-heuristics " <h>"
MaxRects heuristic: \fBBestShortSideFit\fR (default), \fBBestLongSideFit\fR, \fBBestAreaFit\fR, \fBBottomLeft\fR, \fBContactPoint\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-size-constraints " <AnySize|POT>"
Enforce Power-of-Two dimensions (\fBPOT\fR) or arbitrary tight rectangular bounds (\fBAnySize\fR, default).
.TP
.BI \-\-max-size " <width> <height>"
Upper bounds for atlas dimensions (e.g. \fB2048 2048\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-padding " <px>"
Spacing between neighboring sprite rectangles (default: 2).
.TP
.BI \-\-border-padding " <px>"
Padding between sheet outer perimeter and packed sprites (default: 0).
.TP
.BI \-\-extrude " <px>"
Extrude outermost boundary pixels to eliminate texture filtering edge-bleeding (default: 0).
.TP
.BI \-\-trim-mode " <None|Trim|Crop>"
Trimming mode for transparent borders: \fBNone\fR (default), \fBTrim\fR, or \fBCrop\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-trim-threshold " <0-255>"
Alpha threshold below which pixels are considered transparent (default: 1).
.TP
.B \-\-enable-auto-alias
Enable visual deduplication of identical sprites via pixel hashing.
.TP
.BI \-\-pivot-point " <x> <y>"
Normalized anchor point coordinates across sprites [0.0 to 1.0] (e.g. \fB0.5 1.0\fR for ground-feet pivot).
.TP
.BI \-\-godot-uid " <uid>"
Explicit Godot 4 unique identifier string to inject or preserve in generated \fB.tres\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-godot-scene " <file.tscn>"
Generate an instantiable Godot 4 \fBAnimatedSprite2D\fR scene referencing the packed frames.
.TP
.B \-\-multipage
Enable multi-page atlas spanning (M16) when sprite collections exceed maximum page dimensions.
.TP
.BI \-\-texture-format " <png|webp|ktx2|basis>"
Output image encoder format.
.TP
.BI \-\-vram-format " <uastc|etc1s>"
GPU texture compression codec: \fBuastc\fR (high-fidelity HDR/PBR) or \fBetc1s\fR (compact).
.TP
.BI \-\-enable-zstd ", " \-\-disable-zstd
Toggle Zstandard supercompression for KTX2/Basis files (enabled by default).
.TP
.BI \-\-zstd-level " <1-22>"
Zstandard compression level (default: 9).

.SH SLICE OPTIONS (SMART DETECTION)
.TP
.BI \-\-output-dir " <dir>"
Destination folder where segmented PNG frames will be written.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-project " <file.bento>"
Save segmented frames directly as a native BentoPack project.
.TP
.B \-\-remove-bg
Automatically detect and remove uniform background color before segmentation.
.TP
.BI \-\-tolerance " <0-100>"
Color distance tolerance for background removal (default: 10).
.TP
.B \-\-smart-crop
Crop detected bounding boxes tightly around non-transparent pixels.
.TP
.BI \-\-min-size " <px>"
Minimum width and height threshold to discard isolated noise artifacts (default: 3).

.SH FILTER OPTIONS (HEADLESS IMAGE PROCESSING)
.TP
.BI \-\-output " <file.png>"
Destination output image path.
.TP
.BI \-\-despill " [hex_color]"
Remove color bleeding or fringe halos from extracted sprites.
.TP
.BI \-\-outline " [thickness_px]"
Add an outer contour stroke around sprite boundaries.
.TP
.BI \-\-outline-color " <hex_color>"
Hexadecimal color for the outline stroke (e.g. \fI#000000\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-silhouette
Fill sprite interior with solid outline color.
.TP
.BI \-\-color-swap " <#src:#dst>"
Replace a specific source color with a target color while preserving shading.
.TP
.BI \-\-color-adjust
Activate HSL adjustment: use with \fB\-\-hue\fR, \fB\-\-saturation\fR, \fB\-\-contrast\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-pixel-rescale " <2x|3x|4x>"
Nearest-neighbor pixel-art integer upscaling.

.SH WATCH AND DAEMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-watch
Monitor input files and directories and automatically re-pack whenever changes are detected.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Run the watcher in background mode guarded by an atomic directory lockfile (\fI.lock\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-debounce " <ms>"
Debounce latency window in milliseconds before triggering re-packing (default: 300).
.TP
.BI \-\-stop-watch " <dir>"
Gracefully terminate the active watch daemon guarding the specified directory.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
.B ExitSuccess\fR: Execution completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
.B ExitSyntaxError\fR: Invalid arguments, unknown options, or missing required parameters.
.TP
.B 2
.B ExitFileNotFound\fR: Specified input file, directory, or asset does not exist.
.TP
.B 3
.B ExitConstraintFailed\fR: Packing constraints unsatisfied (e.g. frames exceed max dimensions without \fB\-\-multipage\fR).
.TP
.B 4
.B ExitIoError\fR: Disk write error, missing write permissions, or corrupted filesystem.
.TP
.B 5
.B ExitLockConflict\fR: Another watch daemon is already active for this directory.
.TP
.B 6
.B ExitPluginNotFound\fR: Requested format exporter or compressor plugin not available.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.B Pack folder of loose sprites into Godot 4 .tres:
.RS
bentopack-cli --sheet assets/hero.png --data assets/hero.tres --format godot4 sprites/hero/
.RE
.PP
.B Drop-in replacement for TexturePacker with KTX2 VRAM compression:
.RS
TexturePacker --sheet atlas.ktx2 --data atlas.json --format json-array --vram-format uastc input/
.RE
.PP
.B Auto-slice raw sheet with background removal:
.RS
bentopack-cli slice raw_sheet.png --remove-bg --tolerance 12 --output-dir frames/
.RE
.PP
.B Machine-readable schema introspection for AI agent:
.RS
bentopack-cli --schema
.RE

